# Raw trajectory data - large, not tracked (data lives on shared Google Drive)
*.xtc
*.trr
*.cpt
*.tpr
*.gro
*.top
*.itp
*.tar

# Leftover early draft scripts, superseded by plot_<ALLELE>.py
51.py
ee.py
ejef.py

# Unrelated file, not part of this project
CYP3A4_Genetic_Variant_Metabolism.png

# OS clutter
.DS_Store

# MDAnalysis trajectory-offset cache (regenerated automatically, not needed)
.*_offsets.lock
.*_offsets.npz

# GROMACS auto-backup files (e.g. #md_protein.tpr.1#)
\#*\#

# DRN per-frame network output (MD-TASK calc_network.py) -- ~900 files per
# system, too many/large to track; only the final _mean.csv/_mean_*.cif
# summaries are committed.
*.dat

# Protein-only PDB topologies used as calc_network.py input (regenerated
# from md_protein_ref.gro via convert_to_pdb.sh, itself gitignored above)
md_protein_ref.pdb

# Cloned third-party tool (RUBi-ZA/MD-TASK), not project code
MD-TASK/

# Clustering (cpptraj) output is small and useful -- un-ignore from the
# blanket *.dat rule above (which exists for the much larger DRN per-frame
# output).
!cluster_*_summary.dat
!cluster_*_info.dat
!cluster_*_assignments.dat
!cluster_*_rmsd.dat

# Auto-generated cpptraj input scripts, regenerated fresh by
# run_all_clustering.sh each run -- not worth tracking.
cluster_*.in

# PCA eigenvectors (binary, run_all_pca_dccm.sh) and DCCM raw covariance
# matrix (ascii but large, ~15-20MB/system for 463 C-alpha atoms) --
# eigenvalue spectra and PC1/PC2 projections (small) are tracked; the
# per-residue-pair correlation summary from these is written by
# pca_dccm_summary.py and tracked separately.
eigenvec_*.trr
eigenvec_ca_*.trr
covar_*.dat
average.pdb
covar.log

# gmx dssp per-frame secondary structure output (run_all_dssp_gmx.sh).
# Superseded the earlier cpptraj secstruct approach, which produced
# unusable output (broken backbone connectivity in md_protein_ref.pdb ->
# near-zero helix/sheet content everywhere). Per-frame matrix files are
# large (~14MB/system); only the small derived per-residue summaries
# (dssp_*_orderedss.csv, ~5KB/system, written by dssp_summary.py) are
# tracked.
dssp_*.dat

# fpocket/MDpocket binding-pocket analysis outputs (run_all_mdpocket.sh).
#  - md_protein_ref_out/: fpocket pocket detection on the reference
#    structure (all candidate pockets, ~12MB/system)
#  - mdpock_<SYS>_*: MDpocket characterization of the selected active-site
#    pocket (per-frame descriptors + mdpocket_atoms.pdb, ~12MB/system)
#  - mdpout_*: MDpocket exploration density/frequency grids (multi-MB .dx)
#  - selected_pocket_<SYS>.pdb: small, tracked -- defines the active-site
#    pocket per system and is read by pocket_summary.py
#  - md_pocket.xtc: subsampled 601-frame trajectory (covered by *.xtc)
md_protein_ref_out/
mdpock_*
mdpout_*
pocket_traj.*

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OpenCode CLI's own tool state (node_modules, package.json, etc.) -- not
# project/research data, must never be committed.
.opencode/
opencode.jsonc

# CAVER 3.0 substrate access channel analysis (caver_analysis/). Per-system
# raw output is enormous (~270-365MB/system: full snapshot PDBs, per-frame
# tunnel geometry, PyMOL/VMD visualization scripts) and caver_analysis/
# as a whole is ~6.4GB -- far too large to track. Only the small per-system
# summary tables (summary.txt, summary_precise_numbers.csv, each <10KB) are
# kept, since caver_summary.py parses summary.txt directly into the tracked
# caver_summary_all.csv.
caver_analysis/snapshots/
caver_analysis/out_WT/
caver_analysis/logs/
caver_analysis/caver_results/*/analysis/
caver_analysis/caver_results/*/data/
caver_analysis/caver_results/*/pymol/
caver_analysis/caver_results/*/vmd/
caver_analysis/caver_results/*/log.txt
caver_analysis/caver_results/*/warnings.txt
